.TH "KOSH" "5" "October 26, 2026" "kosh" "Koshka Manual"
.SH NAME
kosh \- command\-line options, shell settings, startup scripts, and
KOSHCONF
.PP
Koshka settings files hold option values.
Every shell loads them before any startup file, interactive or not, and
the configured mood also applies to \f[CR]kosh \-c\f[R] and to a script
without a shebang.
The \f[CR]koshconf\f[R] builtin loads, changes, and writes them.
The Shell settings section lists the options.
.PP
The Startup files section lists the shells that apply no settings file
or KOSHCONF.
.SH COMMAND\-LINE OPTIONS
An option given on the command line, on or off, overrides the settings
files and \f[CR]KOSHCONF\f[R].
Koshka\-specific flags appear first, followed by the general, POSIX, and
Bash\-compatible flags.
.PP
