.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]mood\f[R] takes kosh, sh, bash, or bash\-posix.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]completion.menu_style\f[R] takes interactive, external, or plain.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]optimizer.warning_level\f[R] takes 0 to 3.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]editor.base_mode\f[R] takes emacs or vi.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]editor.history.file_path\f[R] and
\f[CR]editor.history.max_entries\f[R] correspond to KOSH_HISTORY_FILE
and KOSH_HISTORY_SIZE.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]editor.wrap_width\f[R] is an integer from 0 to 65535, 80 by
default.
.PP
init_moods is a comma\-separated list of the moods \f[CR]\-L\f[R]
accepts, empty by default, which sources the startup files of the
session mood alone.
It applies only to an interactive or login shell at startup,
\f[CR]\-L\f[R] replaces it, a restricted shell ignores it in the
settings files, and KOSHCONF never carries it.
